      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "What white water?",
      "block": 113
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "Here's where it gets tricky ...",
      "block": 114
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "the falls.",
      "block": 115
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "Where do we go from here?",
      "block": 116
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "We don't.",
      "block": 117
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "I don't understand!",
      "block": 118
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "This is it, as far as we can go ... If we're ",
      "block": 119
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "lucky, they'll be figurin' we can't have ",
      "block": 120
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "come this way and must've beached our ",
      "block": 121
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "canoes and headed cross land. If we're ",
      "block": 122
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "very lucky, they'll figure we went over ",
      "block": 123
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "Then what?",
      "block": 124
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "And if we're unlucky?",
      "block": 125
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "Any powder?",
      "block": 126
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "Only one or two loads.",
      "block": 127
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CORA",
      "quote": "Are we safe?",
      "block": 128
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "Maybe ...",
      "block": 129
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CORA",
      "quote": "Our father? Did you see my father?",
      "block": 130
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CORA",
      "quote": "Tell me!",
      "block": 131
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "CORA",
      "quote": "Say nothing to Alice ...!",
      "block": 132
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "Uncas ...",
      "block": 133
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CORA",
      "quote": "Yes. Go ahead.",
      "block": 134
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "Yes.",
      "block": 135
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "Yes.",
      "block": 136
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "Yes.",
      "block": 137
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "What the bloody hell plan is this?",
      "block": 138
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CORA",
      "quote": "Yes. I want you to go.",
      "block": 139
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CORA",
      "quote": "... never doubt what you are doing.",
      "block": 140
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MAGUA",
      "quote": "Gifts?",
      "block": 141
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "Three, four oxen ... much wampum.",
      "block": 142
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MAGUA",
      "quote": "Wampum?",
      "block": 143
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "Gold could be arranged.",
      "block": 144
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MAGUA",
      "quote": "For Munro children?",
      "block": 145
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MAGUA",
      "quote": "Not enough.",
      "block": 146
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HEYWARD",
      "quote": "What is enough?",
      "block": 147
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "MAGUA",
      "quote": "Heart. Give Magua new heart.",
      "block": 148
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CORA",
      "quote": "Nathaniel!",
      "block": 149
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "(to Sachem)",
      "quote": "I come to you unarmed and in peace to \n\t\t\tunstop your ears, wise one. Because the \n\t\t\tHurons are mislead by the words of the \n\t\t\twolf who's never spoken the truth.",
      "block": 150
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "Let the children of the dead Colonel Munro \n\t\t\tgo free and take the fire out of the English \n\t\t\tanger over the murder of their helpless ones.",
      "block": 151
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "(to Sachem)",
      "quote": "Our father, Montcalm, is greater than the \n\t\t\tYengeese in the arts of war. The Huron \n\t\t\tdo not fear English anger.",
      "block": 152
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "(to Sachem)",
      "quote": "Wise one, the French fathers made peace \n\t\t\tand swore to their honor not to break the \n\t\t\tfriendship. Magua broke it. It is false that \n\t\t\tthe French would not be friends, still, to \n\t\t\tthe Huron.",
      "block": 153
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "(laughs)",
      "quote": "It made our French father happy to never \n\t\t\thave to fight the same Yengeese again. \n\t\t\tHe told me this without telling me this.",
      "block": 154
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "So the Huron are the servants of the French? \n\t\t\tTo do what the French are shamed to do?",
      "block": 155
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MAGUA",
      "quote": "No.",
      "block": 156
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "(to Sachem)",
      "quote": "Huron serve no one. The French father \n\t\t\tbelieves he fooled Magua because he is so \n\t\t\tproud of his cleverness, he is blind. But it \n\t\t\tis the Huron path that Magua walks down, \n\t\t\tnot the French one ... Now, Les Francais, \n\t\t\talso, fear Huron. That is good. When the \n\t\t\tHuron is strong from their fear, we will make \n\t\t\tthe terms of trade with Les Francais. And we \n\t\t\twill trade as the white man trades. Take land \n\t\t\tfrom the Abnakes; fur from the Osage, Sauk \n\t\t\t& Fox. And make the Huron great. Over \n\t\t\tother tribes. No less than the whites, as strong \n\t\t\tas the whites.",
      "block": 157
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "(to Sachem)",
      "quote": "Magua would use the ways of Les Francais \n\t\t\tand the Yengeese ...",
      "block": 158
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "(to Sachem)",
      "quote": "The red man put down the bow, picked up \n\t\t\tthe fire stick and became the best warrior \n\t\t\tin the forest. Yes. It is the only way.",
      "block": 159
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p23",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "(continuing)",
      "quote": "Munro daughter with moon in her hair \n\t\t\tmust be Magua's wife so Munro's seed \n\t\t\tdoesn't die.",
      "block": 160
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p23",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "(continuing; dissolves back to French)",
      "quote": "... and Yengeese officer not go to Les\n\t\t\tFrancais, but back to Yengeese so their \n\t\t\thatred burns less bright. La Longue Carabine, \n\t\t\tgo in peace.",
      "block": 161
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": "p13",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "(to Heyward)",
      "quote": "Tell him I'll trade him! Me for her! Tell him!!",
      "block": 162
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "(shouts)",
      "quote": "I am La Longue Carabine! My death is a \n\t\t\tgreat honor to the Huron. Take me!",
      "block": 163
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "(French; subtitled)",
      "quote": "This is not the voice of wisdom. I go to \n\t\t\tthe Hurons of the Lakes! You are women. \n\t\t\tSend your arrows and guns to the Seneca, \n\t\t\tbeg from them venison to eat, corn to grind. \n\t\t\tSlaves, dogs, rabbits, thieves ... I spit on you!",
      "block": 164
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "I said to trade me!",
      "block": 165
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "(standing)",
      "quote": "What are they doing to Duncan? \n\t\t\tDuncan!",
      "block": 166
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "(low to himself)",
      "quote": "And my compliments to you ...",
      "block": 167
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CORA",
      "quote": "Alice?",
      "block": 168
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "UNCAS!!!",
      "block": 169
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": "p14",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "Will you go back to England?",
      "block": 170
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": "p3",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CORA",
      "quote": "I have nothing to go back for.",
      "block": 171
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": "p14",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "Then will you stay in America?",
      "block": 172
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": "p14",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "And will you be my wife?",
      "block": 173
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": "p3",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CORA",
      "quote": "Yes.",
      "block": 174
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": "p3",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CORA",
      "quote": "Where will we go?",
      "block": 175
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": "p14",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "Winter with the Delaware, my father's ",
      "block": 176
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": "p14",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "cousins. And in the spring, cross the ",
      "block": 177
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": "p14",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "Ohio and look for land to settle with my ",
      "block": 178
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": "p14",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "father in a new place called Can-tuck-ee.",
      "block": 179
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "The frontier moves with the sun and pushes ",
      "block": 180
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "the red man of the wilderness forests in front ",
      "block": 181
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "of it. Until one day there will be nowhere left. ",
      "block": 182
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "Then our race will be no more, or be not us ...",
      "block": 183
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "The frontier place is for people like my white ",
      "block": 184
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "son and his woman and their children.",
      "block": 185
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": "p1",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "That's my father's sadness talking.",
      "block": 186
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": "p3",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "No. It is true ... One day ... there will be no ",
      "block": 187
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": "p3",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "more frontier. Then men like you will go, too. ",
      "block": 188
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": "p3",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "Like the Mohicans. ",
      "block": 189
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": "p3",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "And new people will come. Work. Struggle ",
      "block": 190
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": "p3",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "to make their light ... One mystery remains. ",
      "block": 191
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p3",
      "to": "p1",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "HAWKEYE",
      "quote": "What is that?",
      "block": 192
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": "p3",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "Will there be anything left to show the world ",
      "block": 193
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p1",
      "to": "p3",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CHINGACHGOOK",
      "quote": "that we ever did exist?",
      "block": 194
    }
